  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile RNA with avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) substantially outperforms singleprofile RNA (config_001, acc=0.485), confirming that profile ordering and aggregation matter. Image-only resnet50 (config_010, acc=0.208) is very weak, so RNA remains the primary signal. Question: Does transformer aggregation further improve over avgpool in the multiprofile RNA setting? This experiment (config_003) changes only the aggregation method from avgpool to transformer while holding rna_only, multiprofile, and pca_n2000 fixed, giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_002. Why this is the best next step: It directly tests whether the ordering of multiple profiles carries additional signal beyond their mean, which determines whether we should invest further in more complex aggregation for downstream multimodal experiments. If transformer helps, it justifies transformer-based fusion in multimodal configs; if not, avgpool is sufficient and we can redirect budget toward RNA encoder choice or multimodal fusion."
}

